= jesien_z_marysia
# tlo: jesien_okno
{ podmiana:
    On the first Sunday after Marysia’s return they christened her in the little church in Bukowiec. The godfather was Antek, who throughout the rite kept kneading his brother’s cap in his fingers, and the godmother old Mrs Wójcik. Hanka did not let her daughter out of her arms the whole way there and back.
}
In September asters bloomed under the window. Week by week Marysia grew heavier in their arms and demanded her due ever more loudly, and Hanka sang her the lullaby she had learned from her own mother. # pokaz: kolysanka
But the little one settled quickest when the wind came from the forest and rustled in the thatch – then she would fall silent mid-wail and lie with her eyes open, quiet and grave.
“The woods lull her better than I do,” Hanka would laugh.
Only sometimes, when Jaromir got up in the night to stoke the stove, did he hear the slapping of washing paddles from the direction of the lake.{ sposob_na_odmienca == chrzest_odmienca: It went on until dawn, and one morning Hanka found in the cradle, beside the sleeping Marysia, a handful of wet moss.}
{ uklad_z_mamunami == dar_swietojanski:
    Jaromir did not forget what he had promised at the lake. He knew that in June he would have to carry bread and a wreath to the stone – and every year after that as well.
}
{ uklad_z_mamunami == oddane_lata:
    Hanka noticed that his temples had gone grey like an old man’s, and that of an evening his bones ached, as though more years had been added to him than he had lived.
}
When the first snow fell, howling began to carry from the forest. This time it was a whole pack – and with every night the voices drew nearer to the village. # pokaz: wycie # dalej
